cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "lean4-dom: an executable Lean 4 formalization of WHATWG DOM mutation and live objects"
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Takahashi
    given-names: Masayoshi
repository-code: "https://github.com/takahashim/lean4-dom"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  An executable formalization in Lean 4 of the structural mutation
  algorithms of the WHATWG DOM Standard together with the live objects
  that follow them: live Range, NodeIterator and CharacterData mutation.
  Admissibility of a DOM state is decidable and is proved preserved by
  every modeled operation and by any finite sequence of them. The model
  doubles as an executable oracle for differential testing against the
  Ruby DOM implementation Dommy, which surfaced nineteen conformance
  defects. The formalization also yields a negative result: the live
  Range ordering start <= end, which one would expect to be an
  invariant, is not preserved by insert, and the counterexample is a
  kernel-checked theorem.
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
  - WHATWG DOM
  - differential testing
